{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108219","id":2636489956,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6dJaTk","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108219","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108219.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108219.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108219","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108219/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108219/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108219/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/7b7bd1dceab61b7a5e6b6da10dd091d73549dd50","number":108219,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add Rectangular Area Light Source","user":{"login":"CookieBadger","id":53947784,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzOTQ3Nzg0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53947784?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CookieBadger","html_url":"https://github.com/CookieBadger","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CookieBadger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CookieBadger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CookieBadger/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CookieBadger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CookieBadger/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CookieBadger/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CookieBadger/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CookieBadger/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CookieBadger/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This PR adds a rectangular area light source, implemented via Linearly Transformed Cosines (LTC) with textures. It makes use of a Lookup-Table added in the form of two .dds files, and adds some fields to the `LightData` struct in the light storage, and adds a new atlas for area light textures.\r\n\r\n- Closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/11450.\r\n- Closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/13214\r\n\r\n<img width=\"2047\" height=\"1534\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4de42d95-af99-4949-8fd4-889dd50908cc\" />\r\n\r\n*Image above made by: @passivestar*\r\n\r\n![LTCHeitz_compressed](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/70b67daa-6eea-4e44-80c9-8767cea5f657)\r\n<img width=\"2150\" height=\"1218\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-03-15 004153\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/515501b6-be90-4ac3-b702-bab119e428c9\" />\r\n<img width=\"1237\" height=\"693\" alt=\"black_hole\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e36c0dd0-3c46-4fdb-b6e5-cfb786617765\" />\r\n<img width=\"1572\" height=\"1102\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/627fa2a5-7812-4478-bff7-62dd00dbd0d8\" />\r\n<img width=\"1024\" height=\"890\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9963ed1a-7126-4e16-852a-16098156dffa\" />\r\n\r\n- [x] Integrate lights in VolumetricFog\r\n- [x] Integrate lights in LightMaps\r\n- [x] Integrate lights in VoxelGI\r\n- [x] Integrate lights in SDFGI\r\n- [x] Integrate material effects (Clearcoat, Toon Diffuse & Specular, Rim, Backlight, Transmittance/SSS)\r\n- [x] Implement texturing the light quad\r\n\r\nHere's a list of steps on how to improve the feature in the future:\r\n- Support importing area lights from blender files\r\n- Integrate anisotropy (https://github.com/AakashKT/LTC-Anisotropic/tree/main)\r\n- Integrate in Vertex Shading (if there's a demand)\r\n\r\nHere's how shadows can be improved:\r\n- Add shadows in Compatibility renderer (requires adding paraboloid or alternative shadow mapping to the GLES3 shader).\r\n- Improve accuracy of paraboloid rendering in Forward renderers (currently area lights use the optimized version that was implemented for omni lights, but a more accurate represenation might better prevent leaks)\r\n- Add monte carlo shadows in lightmaps - it would need some parameter for how many rays should be traced. This would be a way to actually get realistic shadows with area lights, so maybe something we would want.\r\n\r\nOne known issue is that specular light can leak through to a face that faces away from the area when viewing at a steep angle and a low roughness value. This is a literal edge case, and fixing it would likely require additional horizon clipping, so maybe we can live with the leak for now. It is present in the source LTC implementation, and the implementation in Unity, and I didn't notice until very recently.\r\n\r\nThe main sources for this technique are https://eheitzresearch.wordpress.com/415-2/ and https://blog.selfshadow.com/publications/s2016-advances/\r\nIn theory, it can be extended to arbitrary polygons, disks, and lines, to serve as the light surface (https://eheitzresearch.wordpress.com/757-2/), but I would worry about adding those in the future.  \r\n\r\nIn the process of making this PR I investigated different techniques for lighting and shading. I investigated a Monte-Carlo sampling approach, and a most-representative point sampling approach, but both were outperformed by LTC, and contemporary research of non-raytraced dynamic area lights still seems to also focus around LTC.\r\nI also investigated shadow sampling with many shadow maps on a new atlas, and adaptive sampling techniques, but those proved to be unusable due to the added implementation complexity. I figured the most suitable shadow technique was using 4 shadow maps per light and directional sampling with PCF to obtain a smooth result, but the shape of the penumbra was strangely warped, and the performance was not good. If you are curious, you may check it out at https://github.com/CookieBadger/godot/tree/area-light-quadriscopic-shadows. Another way to shadow area lights would of course be ray tracing (https://eheitzresearch.wordpress.com/705-2/), but I'm not aware of any developments of the engine in that direction. So, I decided to just integrate PCSS shadows for area lights, which are not physically accurate, but can look decent.\r\n\r\nYou can find a writeup and builds with several example scenes at https://github.com/CookieBadger/master-thesis-artifacts, but those already outdated as they are based on Godot 4.3. You'll also find a Thesis.pdf there, which is my Master's Thesis about this topic.\r\n\r\nAny help with improving and maintaing this feature will be greatly appreciated.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":14236899,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A2Tzj","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/24","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/24","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/24/labels","number":24,"state":"closed","title":"4.7","description":"","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url